{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-stabilizer-preserving}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e11918d255375837d6486aa435452104993f70227cea167b765f7685e66895c8", "source_text": "Stabilizer preserving morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:19feb017e1081c223238458098eb325b498379a7417faa83d7e3d6ae44a96016", "unit_id": "tag:0DU6:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-identify-automorphism-groups}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:88d8ca9996c23ef3ec866a18e50b58e2c5e6ea97093b81bb7943ccf224002839", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2996f0976b89443aa4a17833770afb1816fc9bdb54194a8e89d2489f9ab61564", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the literature a morphism <MATH_0001> of algebraic\nstacks is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>stabilizer preserving<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>fixed-point reflecting<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if the induced morphism\n<MATH_0002>\nis an isomorphism. Such a morphism induces an isomorphism\nbetween automorphism groups (Remark <REF_0001>)\nin every point of <MATH_0003>.\nIn this section we prove some simple lemmas around this concept.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8d2650ea3ac901b6ba1366088d82033073b29a827a8ee2f47618d303e65b97d2", "unit_id": "tag:0DU6:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stabilizer-preserving}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf54fa2da9ae870c4c2ece869f2e0b96e904adef0cf89768a1a5223ade67b0db", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:831480297c48ce9b8ee92b6930080db8fddc1d305d4edac114df522fc514df16", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nIf <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism,\nthen <MATH_0003> is representable by algebraic spaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:622197b9273fc4291ebc63a5a89d83184001c091dc01d872cb8aeb6d8c8aa01b", "unit_id": "tag:0DU7:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-second-diagonal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab519652b2ae80006538759117c8a34235720d631171a776469fb6672315ae62", "source_text": "Immediate from Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ea392ce37d94d2940bc835fcf666bd74b543e3d949c4c2a0a228b09be6bfd4d1", "unit_id": "tag:0DU7:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$G \\to H$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0007": "$G \\to H$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nU \\times_\\mathcal{X} U \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^{\\Delta_f} \\\\\nU \\times_\\mathcal{Y} U \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$G \\to H$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to U \\times U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-separated-implies-isom}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-get-property-auts-from-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:516fd50ae1a324b511d49826bd5e6fb42dfe51054e0eec8376bb2791bc7ad38d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1589d15db7e8483e0cc0567a4d7f649194a36dba34e681fb39d1450c050b4373", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism whose source is an algebraic space.\nLet <MATH_0003> be the pullback of the morphism\n<MATH_0004>\nto <MATH_0005>. If <MATH_0006> is unramified, <ACCENT_0001>tale, etc, so\nis <MATH_0007>. This is true because\n<MATH_0008>\nis cartesian and the morphism <MATH_0009> is the base change of the\nleft vertical arrow by the diagonal <MATH_0010>.\nCompare with the proof of Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b2ed33295ef2f6525359e0c3c69ed9c61cf0afe8fbf3f29ddb7b57f42c41de1", "unit_id": "tag:0DU8:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$f(x)$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-identify-automorphism-groups}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-aut-iso-unramified}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a45d571c372fdd87cb7161a6419db56dbee7d1d8d6dda2c5834d3413dcf4ae75", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1ab92cfb06a00b69a241525b70a70eb4d758d2c6b848f4a1b396010c772c3104", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an unramified\nmorphism of algebraic stacks. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002>\nis an isomorphism, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> induces an isomorphism between automorphism groups at <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>\n(Remark <REF_0001>) for all\n<MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1db3c0e20c154d4179d9fbee1661dc37fbc860e7f40e96ee0fa2cb5421582194", "unit_id": "tag:0DU9:statement"}
